From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OnePlus13-KernelBuilder <builder@kernel>
Date: Fri, 15 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] oplus: gate task-tracker hrtimer on tasktrack_enable

The shipped oplus_bsp_schedinfo.ko unconditionally starts a periodic
hrtimer in tasktrack_init() even though tasktrack_enable defaults to
zero (unless JANK_DEBUG is set).  The handler fires ~7.5 times per
second, immediately returns when the flag is zero, and re-arms.
The proc write handler already starts the timer on enable and cancels
it on disable, so gating the initial start preserves runtime behavior.

Only start the timer if tasktrack_enable is nonzero at init time.

Research: BATTERY_OPTIMIZATION_RESEARCH.md candidate A1.

diff --git a/cpu/sched/sched_info/osi_tasktrack.c b/cpu/sched/sched_info/osi_tasktrack.c
--- a/cpu/sched/sched_info/osi_tasktrack.c
+++ b/cpu/sched/sched_info/osi_tasktrack.c
@@ -771,8 +771,9 @@ void tasktrack_init(void)
 	tasktrack_timer.function = tasktrack_timer_handler;
 
 	jank_update_task_status = jankinfo_update_task_status_cb;
-
+#ifdef JANK_DEBUG
 	tasktrack_timer_start();
+#endif
 
 	return;
 
